Package: hosts-cli
Version: @VERSION@
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: bash (>= 4.4)
Maintainer: N36l3c7 <n36l3c7@protonmail.com>
Homepage: https://n36l3c7.github.io/hosts-cli/
Description: safe command-line manager for /etc/hosts
 /etc/hosts is small enough that everyone edits it by hand, and critical
 enough that a corrupted write breaks name resolution on the whole machine.
 hosts makes the common operations immediate without giving up safety.
 .
 Every change goes to a temporary file in the same directory, is validated,
 and is then moved into place with an atomic rename, so the file holds either
 the whole of the old content or the whole of the new one and never a mixture.
 Owner, group, permissions and SELinux context are carried over, an automatic
 rotated backup is taken before every change, and read commands need no
 privilege at all.
 .
 diffutils and util-linux are used when present, for the diff command and to
 serialise concurrent writers; neither is required for the program to work.
